Overlay patch 0002: build TorchExternal without the non-SF64 game modules.
Torch standalone defaults BUILD_SM64/MK64/FZERO/MARIO_ARTIST=ON; the SM64
factories log raw enum values (BehaviorOpcode/GeoOpcode/LevelOpcode), which
fmt 11 (via 0001's spdlog v1.15.3) rejects: "implicit instantiation of
undefined template fmt::detail::type_is_unformattable_for<...>". The game's
own CMakeLists already builds the vendored torch LIBRARY with SM64/MK64/FZERO
OFF — this aligns the standalone CLI with the in-app extractor's factory set
and dodges the fmt-11-unclean modules we never invoke. SF64 + NAudio stay ON
(SF64 audio extraction uses the NAudio factories).

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -610,6 +610,8 @@
 	PREFIX TorchExternal
     SOURCE_DIR ${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/tools/Torch
     CMAKE_ARGS -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/Torch
+               -DBUILD_SM64=OFF -DBUILD_MK64=OFF -DBUILD_FZERO=OFF
+               -DBUILD_MARIO_ARTIST=OFF
 )
 ExternalProject_Get_Property(TorchExternal install_dir)
 if (MSVC)
